WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:08.109
Tellurium is, is quite a nice element here.
I shall pick it up carefully.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:09.540
Tellurium.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.880
You’ve never had anything to do with this?

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.450
Nothing to do with it in my life. So this
is a new one for me. This is

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:21.290
tellurium powder. So let’s see what’s
inside the vial. So as we open it and

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.220
tap out the glass vial. This one is going
to be stubborn.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:32.390
This bell shape here is a sample of tellurium.
The reason…shall I hold it

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:39.300
for you? … so, a sample of tellurium. I’m
slightly cagey about touching

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.199
this because as I think I explained with selenium
that, if you ingest tellurium into

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:51.170
the body it can get into your sweat and make
you smell enough to really

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:58.100
drive people mad. And these crystals like
this one can be cut up and

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.620
mounted into a piece of apparatus like this.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.320
So a chemist won’t deal with all the elements
on the periodic table in his

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.409
career normally.

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:10.340
No, no, very few chemists will deal with more
than perhaps a

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.420
handful of different elements. So this is
the tellurium and this is, again,

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.300
this is very high standard material. 3 grams
of the tellurium material and

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.920
you can see it’s a very dark powder at the
bottom of the vial.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:32.390
It was used in this piece of apparatus to
shine in an infrared laser that’s

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:38.439
like a heat ray at one frequency and it came
out as twice the frequency.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:43.810
So you can use it to change the effect of
the lasers. Unfortunately the

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:47.659
guy doing it didn’t make a very good job
of it and you can see he’s

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:53.380
completely burnt the surface of this piece
of tellurium. So the main use

00:01:53.380 --> 00:02:03.000
of tellurium is as components like this for
laser optics and it’s not widely

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.490
used in the chemical industry or similar areas.

